course: dictionary
lesson: 13699
title: Words that hurt or numb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Insensitive has two meanings. The first is about people. An insensitive person does not notice or care how others feel, so they say or do hurtful things. «Laughing at Maya's broken arm was insensitive.» Maya was hurt, and the laughing made it worse, even if the other child did not mean to be cruel.
explain: The second meaning is about things that do not react. «The thermometer was insensitive to small changes in temperature» means it did not show the small changes. «Some people are insensitive to cold» means they do not feel it much. Here, the word "to" tells you what the thing does not react to.
explain: To work out which meaning is right, read the words around it. Look for hurt feelings, or for "to" followed by something like pain, light or cold. Then try your meaning in the sentence. Does "not caring how someone feels" fit? Or does "not able to react to" fit better?
fact: Insensitive means not noticing or caring how other people feel, or saying hurtful things.
fact: «An insensitive remark» is a comment that hurts someone's feelings, even when you did not mean it to.
fact: Insensitive can also mean not able to feel or react to something, as in «insensitive to pain».
fact: The noun is «insensitivity». The opposite is sensitive, which means aware of how others feel, or quick to react.
fact: In science, a machine or body part can be «insensitive to small changes», so it does not pick them up.
exercise: «Laughing at Maya's broken arm was insensitive.» What does insensitive mean here? | Clever with numbers | Happy and full of fun | Very quiet and shy | *Careless and hurtful about someone's feelings
exercise: «The thermometer was insensitive to small changes in temperature.» What does insensitive to mean here? | Shouted about | Was afraid of | *Did not react to | Ran very quickly to
exercise: Find the noun in this list that comes from insensitive. | sensitive | feeling | sensation | *insensitivity
test: «Her insensitive comment about his old shoes made Jamal cry.» Why was the comment insensitive? | It was a true fact about the weather | *It hurt his feelings, and she did not think about how he would feel | It was said very quietly | It made Jamal laugh and smile
test: «He was insensitive to the cold, so he went swimming in the sea in winter.» What does this tell you? | He was very afraid of the sea | *He did not feel the cold much | He hated swimming | He was frozen and could not move
exam: Which word is the best synonym for insensitive in the sense of hurtful and careless about feelings? | thoughtful | caring | *thoughtless | gentle
